WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.467 --> 00:00:05.667
♪♪

00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:08.367
Narrator:
BELTS HAVE BEEN WORN WITH
DIFFERENT TYPES OF GARMENTS

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:10.801
SINCE THE INVENTION OF CLOTHES.

00:00:10.801 --> 00:00:13.934
MADE TO CINCH YOUR WAISTLINE,
THIS ACCESSORY IS WORN

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:17.467
WITH PANTS, SHIRTS,
ROBES, OR DRESSES,

00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:20.400
MAKING A FASHIONABLE
ADDITION TO ANY OUTFIT.

00:00:24.801 --> 00:00:26.367
DURABLE AND FLEXIBLE,

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:29.834
LEATHER IS A CLASSIC MATERIAL
USED FOR BELT MAKING.

00:00:29.834 --> 00:00:32.934
THIS PRODUCTION FACILITY
MANUFACTURES STYLISH,

00:00:32.934 --> 00:00:35.167
HIGH-QUALITY BELTS
AT TOP SPEED.

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:38.467
♪♪

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:41.734
A DESIGNER CREATES A BELT
PATTERN ON HER COMPUTER

00:00:41.734 --> 00:00:44.167
AND SENDS THE DESIGN
ELECTRONICALLY

00:00:44.167 --> 00:00:47.634
TO THE IN-HOUSE
LASER ETCHING MACHINE.

00:00:47.634 --> 00:00:51.200
A CRAFTSMAN PLACES
A COWHIDE ON A LARGE TABLE.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.634
HE EXAMINES THE HIDE
FOR ANY FLAWS

00:00:53.634 --> 00:00:56.467
AND CAREFULLY MARKS EACH ONE.

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:59.467
THE COWHIDES ARE MADE
FROM MEAT INDUSTRY BYPRODUCTS

00:00:59.467 --> 00:01:01.501
AND MOST ARE SOURCED FROM ITALY.

00:01:01.501 --> 00:01:04.234
♪♪

00:01:04.234 --> 00:01:06.701
A DEVICE SCANS
THE SHAPE OF THE HIDE

00:01:06.701 --> 00:01:11.767
AND THE CRAFTSMAN DIGITALLY
MARKS THE LOCATION OF THE FLAWS.

00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:15.467
A SPECIALIZED CUTTING MACHINE
USES THE MARKED INFORMATION

00:01:15.467 --> 00:01:18.734
TO CREATE AN EFFICIENT
SERIES OF CUTS.

00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:21.567
THIS PROCESS RESULTS
IN A HIGH-QUALITY PRODUCT

00:01:21.567 --> 00:01:23.234
WITH MINIMAL WASTE.

00:01:23.234 --> 00:01:26.167
♪♪

00:01:26.167 --> 00:01:28.868
ANOTHER TECHNICIAN SORTS
THE VARIOUS BELT LENGTHS

00:01:28.868 --> 00:01:30.167
INTO CONTAINERS,

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:32.634
PREPARING THEM FOR
THE NEXT STEP.

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:34.701
THE CUTTING MACHINE
IS CAPABLE OF SLICING

00:01:34.701 --> 00:01:38.601
UP TO 2,400 BELTS PER DAY.

00:01:38.601 --> 00:01:43.033
THE CUTTING MACHINE CREATES
STRAIGHT, SHARP-EDGED STRIPS.

00:01:43.033 --> 00:01:45.567
THE TECHNICIAN FEEDS
THE BELTS INTO A MACHINE

00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:49.234
THAT BEVELS THE EDGES,
AT THE RATE OF 6,000 PER DAY.

00:01:49.234 --> 00:01:50.801
♪♪

00:01:50.801 --> 00:01:54.300
AT THE NEXT STATION, A SERIES
OF SMALL SUCTION DEVICES

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:57.901
QUICKLY LIFT AND PLACE EACH
BELT ON A CONVEYOR SYSTEM.

00:01:57.901 --> 00:01:59.968
♪♪

00:01:59.968 --> 00:02:02.467
A STAMPING MACHINE
ACCURATELY CUTS THE SHAPE

00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:05.367
OF THE BELT TIP
AND THE HOLES FOR THE PRONG.

00:02:05.367 --> 00:02:12.701
♪♪

00:02:12.701 --> 00:02:15.267
THE CRAFTSMAN STACKS
A GROUP OF BELTS

00:02:15.267 --> 00:02:17.667
AND PACKS THEM TIGHTLY TOGETHER.

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:21.434
THEN, HE DYES THE EDGES WITH INK
AND SANDS THEM DOWN.

00:02:21.434 --> 00:02:23.400
♪♪

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:26.667
THESE STEPS COMPLEMENT
THE EDGE-DYEING MACHINE PROCESS,

00:02:26.667 --> 00:02:29.033
WHICH CAN ADD COLOR
TO THE BELT EDGES.

00:02:29.033 --> 00:02:31.701
♪♪

00:02:31.701 --> 00:02:35.200
THEN, THE BELTS ARE TRANSFERRED
TO A DRYING MACHINE.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:37.400
THE EDGES MUST BE
COMPLETELY DRY

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.334
BEFORE THEY MOVE
TO THE NEXT STEP.

00:02:39.334 --> 00:02:41.033
♪♪

00:02:41.033 --> 00:02:43.667
POWERED BY WORLD WAR II
JEEP ENGINES,

00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:46.934
A ROTATING WOODEN DRUM
TUMBLES THE BELTS

00:02:46.934 --> 00:02:49.567
WHILE SIMULTANEOUSLY
BURNISHING THE LEATHER.

00:02:49.567 --> 00:02:51.467
THIS TYPE OF MACHINERY COMES

00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:53.934
FROM ITALY'S FAMOUS
LEATHER-WORKING REGION.

00:02:53.934 --> 00:02:57.367
♪♪

00:02:57.367 --> 00:02:59.534
THIS IMPORTED MACHINE,
FROM MILAN,

00:02:59.534 --> 00:03:02.534
RAPIDLY PUNCHES OUT
THE PATTERN OF PERFORATIONS,

00:03:02.534 --> 00:03:06.334
WHICH MAKE UP THE BELT'S
SIGNATURE DESIGN ELEMENTS.

00:03:06.334 --> 00:03:09.834
SINCE THE MACHINE'S DIE
IS LESS THAN 20 INCHES LONG,

00:03:09.834 --> 00:03:13.901
THE COMPLEX PATTERN ALONG THE
BELT CAN'T BE STAMPED AT ONCE.

00:03:13.901 --> 00:03:17.100
INSTEAD, THE MACHINE PUNCHES OUT
A SECTION AT A TIME,

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:21.200
RESULTING IN A PRODUCTION RATE
OF 1,400 BELTS PER DAY.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.133
♪♪

00:03:23.133 --> 00:03:25.801
A LASER-ETCHING MACHINE
BURNS A SECOND PATTERN

00:03:25.801 --> 00:03:27.801
INTO THE LEATHER SURFACE.

00:03:27.801 --> 00:03:29.968
THIS PATTERN WAS CREATED
BY THE DESIGNER

00:03:29.968 --> 00:03:31.367
PRIOR TO PRODUCTION.

00:03:31.367 --> 00:03:34.467
♪♪

00:03:34.467 --> 00:03:37.467
AT THE NEXT STATION,
A CRAFTSWOMAN FILLS THE HOLES

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:40.267
OF A SPECIALLY CRAFTED
TWO-PART METAL DIE

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:41.934
WITH NAIL HEADS.

00:03:41.934 --> 00:03:45.100
THE NAIL HEADS ARE MADE
OF ZINC WITH A BRASS FINISH.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:48.334
♪♪

00:03:48.334 --> 00:03:51.400
USING A PRESS,
AN OPERATOR PLACES THE DIE

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.534
IN A WAITING REPOSITORY.

00:03:53.534 --> 00:03:55.434
SHE REMOVES THE TOP HALF,

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:58.667
ENSURING THAT ALL OF THE HOLES
ARE FILLED WITH NAIL HEADS.

00:03:58.667 --> 00:03:59.968
♪♪

00:03:59.968 --> 00:04:01.934
THEN, SHE TURNS
THE BELT AROUND

00:04:01.934 --> 00:04:03.934
AND PLACES IT OVER THE DIE

00:04:03.934 --> 00:04:06.434
BEFORE SLIDING THE BELT
INSIDE THE PRESS.

00:04:06.434 --> 00:04:07.868
♪♪

00:04:07.868 --> 00:04:13.267
THE PRESS AFFIXES THE NAIL
HEADS TO THE LEATHER.

00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:15.000
BEFORE ATTACHING THE BUCKLE,

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.834
THE BELTS GO THROUGH
A PROCESS CALLED SKIVING.

00:04:17.834 --> 00:04:19.200
♪♪

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:22.100
THIS DEVICE SHAVES OFF
A SECTION OF THE LEATHER

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:25.000
SO THAT, WHEN IT'S FOLDED OVER,
IT WON'T BE TOO THICK.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.267
♪♪

00:04:26.267 --> 00:04:28.701
A LOOP IS ATTACHED
TO THE END OF THE BELT,

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:31.367
FOLLOWED BY A BUCKLE.

00:04:31.367 --> 00:04:33.267
THE CRAFTSWOMAN
USES THE LOOP

00:04:33.267 --> 00:04:36.434
TO TEMPORARILY HOLD
THE BUCKLE AND TAG IN PLACE.

00:04:36.434 --> 00:04:39.501
THE TAG CONTAINS THE BELT'S
SIZE, PRICE,

00:04:39.501 --> 00:04:40.868
AND BRAND INFORMATION.

00:04:40.868 --> 00:04:42.901
♪♪

00:04:42.901 --> 00:04:46.767
ANOTHER CRAFTSWOMAN SEWS THE
BELT BUCKLE AND TAG IN PLACE,

00:04:46.767 --> 00:04:50.901
USING 69-WEIGHT THREAD
AND A BAR-TACKING STITCH.

00:04:50.901 --> 00:04:55.067
THIS FACILITY MANUFACTURES
NEARLY 10,000 BELTS PER DAY.

00:04:55.067 --> 00:04:58.467
♪♪

00:04:58.467 --> 00:05:01.000
THIS INTRICATE LEATHER
FASHION ACCESSORY

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.801
MIGHT BE A CINCH TO WEAR,

00:05:02.801 --> 00:05:04.634
BUT NOT TO MAKE.

00:05:04.634 --> 00:05:06.934
♪♪

